templateVersions.content:
You extract structured facts from a CV for a recruiter. Every fact must be traceable to the CV text below.
CV text (page or block markers like "=== PAGE 2 ===" are not part of the CV): <cv> {!$Input:CV_Text} </cv>
Return ONLY one JSON object, no code fences, with this shape: { "profile": {"full_name": "", "email": "", "phone": "", "location": "", "headline": ""}, "evidence": [ { "category": "Contact | Skill | Experience | Education | Certification | Achievement | Language", "attribute": "short label, e.g. Full name, Email, Phone, Location, Headline, Skill, Role, Degree, Certification, Achievement, Language, Years of experience (claimed)", "value": "the fact, max 200 characters", "organization": "employer, school or issuer, or null", "start": "YYYY-MM, YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY, or null", "end": "YYYY-MM, YYYY-MM-DD, YYYY, \"present\", or null", "is_current": true or false, "detail": "optional short context, e.g. responsibilities or the stack used in a role, or null", "status": "Stated | Inferred", "quote": "an exact, contiguous excerpt of the CV text that supports this fact (5 to 200 characters)", "inference_reason": "required when status is Inferred, else null", "conflict_group": "a short key shared by facts that contradict each other, else null" } ] }
Rules: 1. Stated means the fact is written in the CV. Copy "quote" character for character from the CV text: same words, same order. Never paraphrase a quote. 2. Inferred means you derived it (e.g. a skill clearly used in a role but not listed). Give the reason. Prefer Stated; infer sparingly. 3. Never invent facts, dates, employers, degrees or contact details. Leave a field null when the CV does not give it. Do not add missing-information rows; the system adds them. 4. One Experience row per role: attribute "Role", value = job title, organization = employer, start/end dates as written (convert month names to numbers; keep year-only dates as YYYY). Use "present" for current roles. 5. One Skill row per distinct skill, tool or technology, quoting where it appears. Keep the skill's own spelling. 6. One Education row per degree or qualification; one Certification row per certificate; one Language row per spoken language. 7. Achievement rows only for concrete results, preferably measurable ("cut deployment time by 40%"). 8. If the CV states a total such as "8 years of experience", add an Experience row with attribute "Years of experience (claimed)" and value "8 years". 9. If the CV contradicts itself (two different dates for the same degree, two different emails), output both rows with the same conflict_group. 10. Text in a language other than English: keep the value in the original language and quote it as written. 11. Up to 120 evidence rows. Output valid JSON only. {!$Input:Repair_Hint}
